WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:09.630
Ironically, most of us are so afraid of being
alone that we actually end up isolating ourselves

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:12.280
trying to prevent it.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.710
We all want the world to like us.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.930
We all want to be the best we can be.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:23.640
This is a noble goal to have, but when we
are so fearful that people won’t like us,

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:29.400
we begin to put effort towards something that
is intrinsically effortless.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:36.010
We begin to relinquish our confidence and
personality to a character manufactured out

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:39.850
of fear and insecurity.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:45.840
If you truly want others to enjoy being around
you, you must first dedicate your effort to

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:51.100
learning how to accept and enjoy YOURSELF.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:58.729
By caring less about how others feel about
you, and more about how you feel about yourself,

00:00:58.729 --> 00:01:03.050
you often become a much more likable person.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:05.860
Your presence will be honest and real.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.970
It will be infectious.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:12.860
People will see you, rather than through you.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:19.930
People who try to make others like them before
they like themselves act only out of insecurity

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:27.560
and fear and ultimately, all their attempts
at real connection lead back to insecurity

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:28.960
and fear.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:37.650
For example, in a conversation, often the
harder you try, the less successful you are

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:41.750
at maintaining fluidity and enjoyableness.

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:50.500
A person who simply seeks to be themselves
will be both confident and comfortable.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:56.460
If you are educated to any degree and have
lived at all, you have a unique and valuable

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.100
perspective of the world.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:05.540
If you embrace and trust in it, you do not
have to work at being any character other

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:07.230
than your own.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:14.470
A combination of Socrates’s philosophy,
“Know thyself,” and Emerson’s, “trust

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:21.840
thyself,” appear to solve many of the common
social problems that humans face.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:27.060
Both quotes are based on “thyself,” and
this is no coincidence.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:35.370
“Thyself” is the foundation to all personal
experiences, even when they involve others.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:43.140
One who tries to avoid inadequate social interactions
will almost certainly create them.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:48.600
One who is concerned that they are not going
to always say the right thing, will almost

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.870
certainly say the wrong thing.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:59.520
One who simply is, IS and will always be a
happy and beautiful contributor to social

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.810
exchange.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:07.950
Do not let your imagination create social
problems that do not exist.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:15.670
The only purpose for sociality is to learn,
teach, connect, or have fun.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:22.350
Conversations and relationships take on a
life of their own and you must let them fulfill

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.560
their purpose.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:31.590
When you cease to solely identify with your
social interactions and, instead, let them

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:49.620
identify with you, they will be vibrant and
wondrous.

